# __PROJECT__

C++__CPP_STANDARD__ project using MSVC x64, CMake 3.28+ and Ninja, with a
`libs/core` library target, a thin `app` executable, and Catch2 tests.
Use VS Code, Neovim or Visual Studio. Install the compiler/Windows SDK and CMake/Ninja;
the build helper discovers an existing C++ installation and does not install tools.

```powershell
./scripts/Build.ps1 -Test
./build/dev/bin/__PROJECT__.exe
./scripts/Build.ps1 -Configuration Release
./scripts/Build.ps1 -Configuration Asan -Test
```

Or run `./scripts/Enter-DevShell.ps1`, then use the CMake `dev` and `release` presets
directly; for `asan`, enter with `-Component Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.ASAN` so an
installation with the "C++ AddressSanitizer" component is selected. Run sanitized binaries
from that shell, which puts the ASan runtime DLL on `PATH`. An editor launched from that
shell inherits the environment. clangd reads `build/dev/compile_commands.json` for the
scaffold's `app`, `libs`, and `tests` source roots; `.vscode/launch.json` debugs the `dev`
build. If another build system owns another source root, generate its compilation database
and add a path-scoped entry to `.clangd`; the C/C++ extension's compile-commands setting does
not configure clangd.

The initial targets use the dynamic MSVC CRT, exceptions, and warnings as errors for owned
code. Warnings and AddressSanitizer are applied through the `__NAMESPACE___warnings` and
`__NAMESPACE___sanitize` interface targets, so they affect only this project's targets; the
`asan` preset enables the sanitizer. Record the actual compiler and SDK versions after
building. C++23 may map to `/std:c++latest` in a particular CMake/MSVC pairing; inspect the
actual compiler command. Choose and test runtime/deployment settings when the application
gains consumers. `cmake --install build/dev` copies the executable into
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\WindowsApps` unless you pass `--prefix`.

The sample `core::greeting()` function and its Catch2 case exist only to prove the scaffold
builds and tests end to end — replace them with real logic. `-Fresh` reconfigures after a
toolchain change. Use separate build directories/presets for different architectures or
generators.
